# Getting Started

This guide will help you get up and running with the Fanbasis Payment SDK in just a few minutes.

## Prerequisites

Before you begin, make sure you have:

- A Fanbasis merchant account
- Node.js 16+ installed
- A modern web browser
- Basic knowledge of JavaScript/TypeScript

## Installation

### For React Applications

```
npm install @fanbasis/checkout-react
```

### For Vanilla JavaScript

```
npm install @fanbasis/checkout-core
```

## Quick Start Options

### 🚀 Hosted JavaScript (Fastest)

For the quickest integration without any build process, use our hosted JavaScript solution.

### React (Recommended for React Apps)

**1. Wrap your app with CheckoutProvider**

```
import React from 'react';
import { CheckoutProvider, AutoCheckout } from '@fanbasis/checkout-react';

const config = {
  creatorId: 'your-creator-id',
  productId: 'your-product-id',
  checkoutSessionSecret: 'your-session-secret',
  environment: 'sandbox'
};

function App() {
  return (
    <CheckoutProvider config={config}>
      <AutoCheckout autoOpen={true} />
    </CheckoutProvider>
  );
}

export default App;
```

**2. That's it!** Your checkout is now ready to use.

### Vanilla JavaScript

**1. Create a checkout instance**

```
import { PaymentCheckout } from '@fanbasis/checkout-core';

const checkout = PaymentCheckout.create({
  creatorId: 'your-creator-id',
  productId: 'your-product-id',
  checkoutSessionSecret: 'your-session-secret',
  environment: 'sandbox'
});
```

**2. Attach to DOM and open**

```
// Get a container element
const container = document.getElementById('checkout-container');

// Attach and open
checkout.attachToElement(container);
await checkout.init();
```

**3. Handle events**

```
checkout.on('checkout:success', (data) => {
  console.log('Payment successful:', data);
});

checkout.on('checkout:error', (error) => {
  console.error('Payment failed:', error);
});
```

## Configuration

### Required Configuration

You need these values from your Fanbasis dashboard:

- **creatorId**: Your unique creator identifier
- **productId**: The product you want to sell
- **checkoutSessionSecret**: A secure session secret
- **environment**: Either 'sandbox' or 'production'

### Getting Your Credentials

1. Log in to your Fanbasis merchant dashboard
2. Navigate to the API section
3. Copy your creator ID and generate a session secret
4. Create or select a product to get the product ID

### 🔑 Need Help with Session Secrets?

Learn how to create and manage checkout session secrets for your integration.

### Environment Setup

```
// Development/Sandbox
const config = {
  creatorId: 'your-creator-id',
  productId: 'your-product-id',
  checkoutSessionSecret: 'your-session-secret',
  environment: 'sandbox'
};

// Production
const config = {
  creatorId: 'your-creator-id',
  productId: 'your-product-id',
  checkoutSessionSecret: 'your-session-secret',
  environment: 'production'
};
```

## Testing

### Sandbox Testing

The sandbox environment allows you to test payments without real money:

- Use test credit card numbers
- No actual charges are made
- Full API functionality is available
- Debug information is provided

### Test Credit Cards

Use these test card numbers in sandbox mode:

- **Visa**: 4242 4242 4242 4242
- **Mastercard**: 5555 5555 5555 4444
- **American Express**: 3782 822463 10005
Use any future expiration date and any 3-4 digit CVC.

## Complete Examples

### React Example

```
import React, { useState } from 'react';
import { CheckoutProvider, AutoCheckout } from '@fanbasis/checkout-react';

function CheckoutPage() {
  const [paymentSuccess, setPaymentSuccess] = useState(false);

  const config = {
    creatorId: 'your-creator-id',
    productId: 'product_456',
    checkoutSessionSecret: 'secret_789',
    environment: 'sandbox',
    theme: {
      theme: 'light',
      accent_color: '#007bff'
    }
  };

  const handleSuccess = (data) => {
    setPaymentSuccess(true);
    console.log('Payment successful:', data);
  };

  const handleError = (error) => {
    console.error('Payment error:', error);
  };

  if (paymentSuccess) {
    return (
      <div>
        <h2>Payment Successful!</h2>
        <p>Thank you for your purchase.</p>
      </div>
    );
  }

  return (
    <CheckoutProvider config={config}>
      <div>
        <h1>Complete Your Purchase</h1>
        <AutoCheckout
          autoOpen={true}
          onSuccess={handleSuccess}
          onError={handleError}
        />
      </div>
    </CheckoutProvider>
  );
}

export default CheckoutPage;
```

### Vanilla JavaScript Example

```
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Fanbasis Checkout</title>
    <style>
        #checkout-container {
            min-height: 500px;
            border: 1px solid #ddd;
            border-radius: 8px;
            margin: 20px 0;
        }
        .button {
            background: #007bff;
            color: white;
            border: none;
            padding: 12px 24px;
            border-radius: 4px;
            cursor: pointer;
            font-size: 16px;
        }
        .button:hover {
            background: #0056b3;
        }
        .button:disabled {
            background: #6c757d;
            cursor: not-allowed;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <div id="app">
        <h1>Product Checkout</h1>
        <p>Click the button below to start your purchase.</p>

        <button id="open-checkout" class="button">
            Open Checkout
        </button>

        <div id="checkout-container"></div>

        <div id="status"></div>
    </div>

    <script type="module">
        import { PaymentCheckout } from '@fanbasis/checkout-core';

        // Configuration
        const config = {
            creatorId: 'your-creator-id',
            productId: 'product_456',
            checkoutSessionSecret: 'secret_789',
            environment: 'sandbox',
            theme: {
                theme: 'light',
                accent_color: '#007bff',
                show_product_info: true,
                product_layout: 'left'
            }
        };

        // Create checkout instance
        const checkout = PaymentCheckout.create(config);

        // Get DOM elements
        const openButton = document.getElementById('open-checkout');
        const container = document.getElementById('checkout-container');
        const status = document.getElementById('status');

        // State
        let isOpen = false;

        // Update button state
        function updateButton() {
            openButton.textContent = isOpen ? 'Close Checkout' : 'Open Checkout';
            openButton.disabled = false;
        }

        // Show status message
        function showStatus(message, type = 'info') {
            status.innerHTML = `<div style="padding: 10px; margin: 10px 0; border-radius: 4px; background: ${type === 'error' ? '#f8d7da' : '#d4edda'}; color: ${type === 'error' ? '#721c24' : '#155724'};">${message}</div>`;
        }

        // Event handlers
        checkout.on('checkout:opened', () => {
            isOpen = true;
            updateButton();
            showStatus('Checkout opened successfully');
        });

        checkout.on('checkout:closed', () => {
            isOpen = false;
            updateButton();
            showStatus('Checkout closed');
        });

        checkout.on('checkout:loaded', () => {
            showStatus('Checkout loaded and ready');
        });

        checkout.on('checkout:success', (data) => {
            showStatus(`Payment successful! Transaction ID: ${data.transactionId}`);
            isOpen = false;
            updateButton();
        });

        checkout.on('checkout:error', (error) => {
            showStatus(`Payment failed: ${error.message}`, 'error');
            isOpen = false;
            updateButton();
        });

        // Button click handler
        openButton.addEventListener('click', async () => {
            try {
                if (isOpen) {
                    checkout.destroy();
                } else {
                    openButton.disabled = true;
                    openButton.textContent = 'Opening...';

                    checkout.attachToElement(container);
                    await checkout.init();
                }
            } catch (error) {
                console.error('Checkout error:', error);
                showStatus(`Error: ${error.message}`, 'error');
                updateButton();
            }
        });

        // Initialize
        updateButton();
    </script>
</body>
</html>
```

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues

1. **"Creator ID is required"**
  - Make sure you've provided a valid creator ID
  - Check that the ID is correct in your dashboard
2. **"Product ID is required"**
  - Ensure you've specified a valid product ID
  - Verify the product exists in your dashboard
3. **"Checkout session secret is required"**
  - Generate a new session secret in your dashboard
  - Make sure it's not expired
4. **Checkout not opening**
  - Ensure the container element exists in the DOM
  - Check that the container has sufficient dimensions
  - Verify your internet connection

### Getting Help

If you run into issues:

1. Check the browser console for error messages
2. Verify your configuration is correct
3. Test in sandbox mode first
4. Review the [API Reference](/docs/api-reference) for detailed information

### Support

For additional help:

- Check the [Examples](/docs/examples) for more use cases
- Review the [API Reference](/docs/api-reference) for detailed documentation
- Contact support through your Fanbasis dashboard

